{
  "requirement": "The `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "**Judgment: the requirement is met.** The requirement says the `habeas` CLI MUST use `clap` to define and parse its commands and options.\n\n**Implementation**\n- `src/main.rs` imports `clap::{ArgGroup, Parser, Subcommand}`, and `Cargo.toml` declares `clap` 4.6.7 with the `derive` feature.\n- `struct Cli` (lines 10–16) derives `Parser`.\n- `enum Command` (lines 18–85) derives `Subcommand`. It defines `mdbook`, `setup`, `status`, `info`, `author` (with the `author-evidence` alias), the hidden `hook`, and `add-input`. Their options, positional arguments and `ArgGroup` constraints are all declared through clap attributes.\n- `enum MdbookCommand` and `enum HookCommand` also derive `Subcommand`.\n- `main` calls `Cli::parse()` (line 100), and all dispatch goes through the parsed `Command`.\n- A search of `src` for `env::args`, `args_os` and `.args()` found no hand-rolled argument parsing, so nothing implementing the requirement is left unmarked.\n- Each of these sites carries `{impl}` for `requirements.cli.clap`.\n- The extra `{impl}` markers in `Command` and `main` point at other requirements, such as `authoring.*` and `cli.add_input*`. They don't add behaviour this requirement leaves unspecified.\n\n**Tests**\n- `tests/cli.rs::clap_defines_commands_options_and_usage_errors` runs the real binary and checks:\n  - `--help` output starts with `Usage: habeas <COMMAND>` and lists every public command.\n  - The hidden `hook` command is absent from help.\n  - `status --help` shows `--all` and `--verbose`.\n  - The `author-evidence` alias parses to the `author` command.\n  - Usage errors exit with code 2 and print the clap message and a usage line. The three cases are an unknown option (`status --bogus`), a missing required argument (`info`), and conflicting arguments (`author x --all`).\n- `tests/commands.rs::add_input_requires_one_target_and_mode_and_resets_changed_records` covers the clap `ArgGroup` constraints on `add-input`. For missing or doubled targets and modes, it asserts exit code 2 and `Usage: habeas add-input`, and that nothing is written.\n\nTogether these tests cover the positive path (commands, options and alias defined and parsed by clap) and the failure paths (usage errors). I found no remaining gaps.",
